        "",
        "**Compilation Speed Analysis (`wazig.6` vs `wazigl.6` vs `zig 0.17.0`):**",
        f"- **`wazig v0.17.0-wazig.6` (`-fno-llvm`) vs `wazigl v0.17.0-wazigl.6` (`-fllvm`)**: Because `wazig` uses Zig's self-hosted WebAssembly backend (`src/codegen/wasm/CodeGen.zig` + `src/link/Wasm/component/Optimizer.zig`) without invoking LLVM's optimization passes, `wazig.6` compiles **1.92x–4.47x faster** than `wazigl.6` across every workload (`{w['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` vs `{wl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` warm on `wasm_bench_runner ReleaseSmall`, `{w['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['warm']:.2f}s` vs `{wl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['warm']:.2f}s` warm on `ReleaseFast +simd128`, `{w['compile_sec']['tests_12_wasi']['wall_parallel_sec']:.2f}s` vs `{wl['compile_sec']['tests_12_wasi']['wall_parallel_sec']:.2f}s` wall time across all `wasm32-wasi` test suites, and `{w['compile_sec']['fmt_check']:.3f}s` vs `{wl['compile_sec']['fmt_check']:.3f}s` on `fmt --check`).",
        f"- **`wazig v0.17.0-wazig.6` vs Native `zig v0.17.0 -fllvm`**: Even running inside Wasmtime (`wasm64-wasip3`), `wazig.6` warm-cache builds (`{w['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` `ReleaseSmall`, `{w['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast']['warm']:.2f}s` `ReleaseFast`, `{w['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['warm']:.2f}s` `ReleaseFast +simd128`) are **faster than or competitive with native `zig 0.17.0 -fllvm`** (`{zl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` `ReleaseSmall`, `{zl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast']['warm']:.2f}s` `ReleaseFast`, `{zl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['warm']:.2f}s` `ReleaseFast +simd128` — **up to {zl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['warm'] / w['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['warm']:.2f}x faster**), and `triangle` (`{w['compile_sec']['triangle_release']['warm']:.2f}s` vs `{zl['compile_sec']['triangle_release']['warm']:.2f}s` warm) and `embedded` (`{w['compile_sec']['embedded_release']['warm'] if isinstance(w['compile_sec']['embedded_release'], dict) else w['compile_sec']['embedded_release']:.2f}s` vs `{zl['compile_sec']['embedded_release']['warm'] if isinstance(zl['compile_sec']['embedded_release'], dict) else zl['compile_sec']['embedded_release']:.2f}s` warm) build faster than native LLVM.",
        f"- **`wazigl v0.17.0-wazigl.6` vs Native `zig v0.17.0 -fllvm`**: Running the full LLVM 22 + Clang C++ toolchain inside Wasmtime (`wazigl.wasm`, `193.02 MiB`) incurs a ~2.7x–2.9x Wasmtime guest execution multiplier relative to native `zig -fllvm` (`{wl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` vs `{zl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` warm on `ReleaseSmall`, `{wl['compile_sec']['playground_release_webgpu_st']['warm'] if isinstance(wl['compile_sec']['playground_release_webgpu_st'], dict) else wl['compile_sec']['playground_release_webgpu_st']:.2f}s` vs `{zl['compile_sec']['playground_release_webgpu_st']['warm'] if isinstance(zl['compile_sec']['playground_release_webgpu_st'], dict) else zl['compile_sec']['playground_release_webgpu_st']:.2f}s` warm on `playground ReleaseSmall`), making `wazig.6` ideal for fast CI test/check inner loops and `wazigl.6` ideal when maximum LLVM codegen optimization is desired without OS/arch-specific native compiler binaries.",
        "",
