        f"  - In **`ReleaseFast +simd128`** builds, `wazig.6` (`{fmt_kb(w['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'])}` raw / `{fmt_kb(w['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['zstd'])}` zstd) is **{wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'] / w['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw']:.2f}x smaller** than `wazigl.6` (`{fmt_kb(wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'])}` raw / `{fmt_kb(wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['zstd'])}` zstd) and `zig 0.17.0 -fllvm` (`{fmt_kb(zl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'])}` raw / `{fmt_kb(zl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['zstd'])}` zstd), because LLVM's `ReleaseFast` loop unrolling and aggressive inlining expand `.wasm` binary size by **{wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'] / wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['raw']:.2f}x** over `ReleaseSmall` (`{fmt_kb(wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['raw'])}` → `{fmt_kb(wl['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'])}`), whereas `wazig.6`'s targeted 2-pass inliner and MIR/linker optimizations (`Optimize.zig` + `Optimizer.zig`, `cataggar/zig#214`/`#217`/`#223`/`#224`) add only `+14.1%` over `ReleaseSmall` (`{fmt_kb(w['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['raw'])}` → `{fmt_kb(w['binary_sizes']['wasm_bench_runner_releasefast_simd']['raw'])}`).",
